Takes the buttons of a mouse or a trackpad on iPadOS, Mac Catalyst and visionOS from the pointer of UIKit while the scene of the window does not lock the pointer, since UIKit reports the clicks of every source, such as a mouse, a trackpad, Voice Control, Switch Control, remote control and UI tests, while GameController reads only the mice of the hardware. SDL read the buttons and the wheel of every mouse that GameController knows from GameController alone, so no other click reached the app. The view keeps the lock state of the scene from the notifications of UIKit, the buttons come from the pointer of UIKit unless the scene locks the pointer, and GameController reports the buttons and the wheel only while the scene locks it, when UIKit reports neither, and on tvOS, which has no pointer of UIKit. The runtime reads the scrolls of a pointer that the scene does not lock from UIKit itself.

